{"id":"466d3f3a-3ef0-45b9-b5f4-1f792b7adfff","object":"chat.completion","created":1785035783,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dict\\\")\\n    if \\\"threshold\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing threshold\\\")\\n    if \\\"calls\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"missing calls\\\")\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be a number\\\")\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each call must be a dict\\\")\\n        required = [\\\"call_id\\\", \\\"loss_without_call\\\", \\\"loss_with_call\\\", \\\"prediction_tokens\\\", \\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        for key in required:\\n            if key not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"missing {key}\\\")\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"call_id must be a string\\\")\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        pred_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_without_call must be a number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss_with_call must be a number\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(pred_tokens, int) or pred_tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be a boolean\\\")\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement solve(case) according to the specification. The case payload has \"threshold\" (number) and \"calls\" (array of objects). Each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable. We need to compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens (at least one prediction token, but we have prediction_tokens positive integer? The spec says \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" meaning we divide by prediction_tokens. Then we check if parseable is True and normalized_gain >= threshold. If both true, the call is accepted. Then we output accepted_call_ids (list of strings) and diagnostics (list of objects with accepted, call_id, normalized_gain; normalized_gain should be a number, presumably float). Order of diagnostics should match input order. Return exactly the structure required. Also note: The threshold is given, we use it directly. No rounding is specified? The output schema says normalized_gain type: number, no rounding constraint. But the candidate_artifact mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" and \"Return only JSON-serializable values\". Maybe they expect rounding? The text says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" So we should round normalized_gain to some precision? It doesn't specify. Since it's just \"number\", we can keep as float. But to be safe, we might round to something like 8 decimal places? However, the examples in the fixture payload have floats with 8 decimals. The output should probably be similar. But the spec doesn't enforce rounding, so we can just compute and return the float without rounding. However, the candidate artifact says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\". Could be a soft preference. But the explicit output structural schema says \"type: number\", no rounding. I'll compute as float. The task says \"Use only quantities present in the case payload.\" So no external rounding function needed. I'll just compute gain/prediction_tokens as float.\n\nWe need to raise ValueError for infeasible or structurally invalid case. That's for cases where input is missing fields or types don't match. We'll validate: threshold is number, calls is list, each call has required fields and proper types. If any field missing or wrong type, raise ValueError.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case) that does validation, iterates over calls, computes normalized_gain, checks accepted, builds diagnostics list and accepted_call_ids list. Return dict with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nAlso note: The spec says \"Keep diagnostics in supplied call order.\" So we maintain order as we iterate.\n\nNo mutation of case. Use Python standard library only. Return JSON-serializable object.\n\nNow produce the implementation as a JSON string with key \"implementation\". The entire response must be that JSON object. No extra text.\n\nWe'll output:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n\nMake sure to escape newlines and quotes properly.\n\nLet's write the code.\n\nPseudo:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate fields\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\n        raise ValueError(\"case must be a dict\")\n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing threshold\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing calls\")\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(\"threshold must be number\")\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be list\")\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"each call must be dict\")\n        required = [\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"]\n        for key in required:\n            if key not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"missing {key}\")\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\n            raise ValueError(\"call_id must be string\")\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        pred_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        # Validate types\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"loss_without_call must be number\")\n        if not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"loss_with_call must be number\")\n        if not isinstance(pred_tokens, int) or pred_tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive int\")\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\n            raise ValueError(\"parseable must be bool\")\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\n        accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat should work.\n\nNow produce the final JSON response."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2164,"completion_tokens":1724,"total_tokens":3888,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1130},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":116},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}